> [IAudioClient3](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/audioclient/nn-audioclient-iaudioclient3) is supported on Windows 10 only, interface won't be defined on older SDKs and MinGW and will fail to build.

@bruvzg was correct about MinGW failing to compile; the audioclient.h distributed with MinGW doesn't define the IAudioClient3 interface. With this in mind I made some modifications and have successfully cross-compiled IAudioClient3 support from Ubuntu in addition to MinGW on Windows 7. I tested this build on both Windows 7 and Windows 10 with the intended behaviour on the respective platforms. 

I'll update the PR with this and the requested change as soon as I can.
